<Base title="Build with apps you own" description="Get your environment ready, choose useful mini-apps, and let your coding agent build software you own. Configure independent apps and connect their data."><section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow font-display">App Composer / on Cloudflare</p><h1>Build with <br/><span>apps you own.</span></h1><p class="lede">Connect a photo guestbook to a curated collection. Configure the result, then let your agent handle the build and deployment.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/ready">Get ready to build <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/demo">See the apps working together</a></div><p class="note">You can explore the apps and save a draft before signing in.</p></div><svg class="hero-art" viewBox="0 0 580 530" role="img" aria-label="Two independent source apps join a shared route: a guestbook contribution becomes a featured showcase item. Each app keeps its own source and data."><rect x="50" y="25" width="340" height="230" rx="14" fill="#ff9b55"/><rect x="200" y="230" width="330" height="265" rx="14" fill="#343940"/><path d="M140 125H450V345H300" fill="none" stroke="#17181b" stroke-width="18" class="line"/><path d="M140 125H450V345H300" fill="none" stroke="#ff9b55" stroke-width="6" class="line"/><circle cx="140" cy="125" r="22" fill="#252923"/><circle cx="450" cy="345" r="22" fill="#f4f0e8"/><circle cx="300" cy="345" r="22" fill="#ff9b55"/><text x="78" y="78" fill="#252923" font-size="25">Here / there</text><text x="78" y="220" fill="#252923" font-size="18">A moment, approved.</text><text x="230" y="285" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="25">Good company</text><text x="230" y="454" fill="#f4f0e8" font-size="18">That moment, featured.</text></svg></section><section class="section split"><div><h2>Collect a photo. Give it a place.</h2><p class="lede">Leave a moment in Here / there. Approve it, feature it in Good company, then open the original. Hide the source and the feature disappears.</p><a class="button" href="/demo">Open the live composition</a><p class="note">Each app keeps its own GitHub source and data.</p></div><div class="demo-images"><figure><a href="/guestbook"><img src="/brand/guestbook.png" alt="Original guestbook artwork: warm abstract shapes at an orange interchange" width="600" height="600"/></a><figcaption>Here / there · Photo Guestbook</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="/showcase"><img src="/brand/showcase.png" alt="Original showcase artwork: selected shapes arranged on a deep green field" width="600" height="600"/></a><figcaption>Good company · Curated Showcase</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Choose your next step.</h2><div class="route-row"><h3>No idea yet?</h3><p>Your coding agent checks your actual workspace, GitHub and Cloudflare, then deploys a small HTTPS reference. Real proof comes before a project brief.</p><a href="/ready">Get Ready</a></div><div class="route-row"><h3>Ready to make?</h3><p>Choose apps and configure the parts that matter. Export a portable spec and hand it to Codex in the environment you already verified.</p><a href="/init">Start Init</a></div><div class="route-row"><h3>Still deciding?</h3><p>Compare directions, change your mind and save a decision path. Exploration does not purchase, deploy or change your account.</p><a href="/explore">Explore decisions</a></div></section><section class="section split"><div><h2>Keep your source and customisations.</h2><p>Each app keeps its source history and current privacy state. Configuration stays separate from upstream code. A failed update leaves the working version in place.</p><a href="/docs">Read the ownership and update model</a></div><div class="ink"><h3>You set the direction.</h3><p class="lede">Your agent prepares the environment, builds the app and checks the deployment. You keep the final say.</p><p>Authentication, purchases and consequential approvals still belong to you. The agent handles routine technical decisions.</p></div></section></Base>
